            <ArticleTitle>Seronegative arthritis as a cause of heel pain.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>369-75</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Seronegative disease as a cause of heel pain is not nearly as common as mechanically induced heel pain. Recognizing the clinical findings, however, will help in distinguishing this from more common forms of heel pain.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
